    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_planar - Edgecase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_planar.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_planar()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Place the nodes of a planar graph so that no edges cross.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_planar()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Place the nodes of a planar graph so that no edges cross.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_planar()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Place the nodes of a planar graph so that no edges cross.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes of a planar graph so that no edges cross.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L5687-L5776){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_planar(\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Planar layout](../assets/graphs/layout-planar.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, the octahedron graph (six nodes, each joined to four others) scattered at random, with several edges crossing. On the right, layout_planar() draws it with no crossings: a large outer triangle of nodes 1, 2 and 4 with the other three nodes inside it.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nFinds a planar embedding (see `check_planarity()`), adds edges to make it 2-connected\nand to triangulate every face but the largest, which becomes the outer face, and then\nplaces the nodes one at a time in a canonical order with the shift method of Chrobak and\nPayne. Every node lands on an integer grid point, `x` from `0` to `2n - 4` and `y` from\n`0` to `n - 2`, and the edges drawn as straight lines never cross. The result is\ncentered and scaled so the largest coordinate is `scale=`. This ports NetworkX's\n`planar_layout()`; a planar graph has many embeddings and this one need not be the one\nNetworkX finds, so the positions can differ from NetworkX's while being just as\ncrossing-free.\n\nThe drawing guarantees no crossings, not good looks: the triangulation pulls the nodes\ninto a broad triangle, and nodes deep inside it can sit close together. It suits\nchecking or showing that a graph is planar; for a readable picture, a force-directed\nlayout such as `layout_spring()` often draws a planar graph without crossings too.\nEdge direction, self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Graphs with fewer than four\nnodes use fixed points of a triangle, `(0, 0)`, `(2, 0)` and `(1, 1)`, in node ID order,\nand separate components are joined before triangulating, so they are laid out together.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Largest coordinate after rescaling. `None` keeps the integer grid coordinates\n    (`center=` is then ignored). Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the layout, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is not planar (see `is_planar()`), or `scale=` or `center=` is\n    invalid.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~check_planarity`) \n\n:   The planar embedding this layout draws.\n\n[](`~is_planar`) \n\n:   Whether a graph can be drawn without crossings at all.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\n`K_4` is planar, so it can be drawn without crossings, with one node inside the triangle\nof the other three. `scale=None` keeps the grid coordinates:\n\n::: {#2fbbf657 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nec.Graph().add_full_graph(n=4).layout_planar(scale=None, return_dict=True)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{1: (0.0, 0.0), 2: (4.0, 0.0), 3: (2.0, 1.0), 4: (2.0, 2.0)}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nStored positions are what `plot(layout=...)` draws:\n\n::: {#6dd9e30b .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nec.Graph().add_named_graph(\"dodecahedral\").layout_planar().plot(layout=\"pos\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"14.0 15.1 672.0 480.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"14.0\" y=\"15.1\" width=\"672.0\" height=\"480.0\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<line x1=\"161.5\" y1=\"293.5\" x2=\"71.3\" y2=\"383.7\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-1-0\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"184.1\" y1=\"270.9\" x2=\"258.1\" y2=\"196.9\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-10-1\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"187.7\" y1=\"288.0\" x2=\"192.1\" y2=\"289.7\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-12-2\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"559.1\" y1=\"381.5\" x2=\"624.2\" y2=\"392.4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-2-3\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"529.0\" y1=\"371.7\" x2=\"525.4\" y2=\"369.9\" stroke=\"#